abstract: >-
  A source-based case study of institutional digital asset custody, examining
  signing authority, policy enforcement, distributed state, recovery trust,
  and the implications of quantum attacks on elliptic curve signatures.
  Reproducible application tests, declared models, a synthetic local-chain
  transfer, and verification microbenchmarks accompany a proposed migration
  architecture. Published independently as a preprint on Zenodo. No peer-review
  status or production custody certification is claimed.
